            <ArticleTitle>Delayed spontaneous recanalization of a totally occluded right coronary artery following failed percutaneous coronary intervention with associated Type F dissection: case report and review.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>174-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary artery dissection is a well-known and frequent complication of percutaneous coronary intervention (PCI). We report the first case of a Type F dissection following PCI of the distal right coronary artery causing total vessel occlusion that could not be stented but was associated with late spontaneous recanalization and a favorable outcome.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
